<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldSailScatterer.xml             UtinniPatches · SCALD_MECHANICS_1 S5
  ============================================================================
  scald_kit_spec.md S5 "bubble-sailors": "placed at gen by
  RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces keyed to RUT_ScaldVent sites — each vent gets a
  sail cluster... Tethering: RM_CompTerritorialAnchor anchored to the vent —
  sails never leave their bubble line (INVENTED: radius 8), ignore
  everything, flee nothing." RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces and
  RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn are REUSED verbatim, not rebuilt — both
  already shipped in MIASMA_MECHANICS_1's M6 build pass (read in full before
  writing this file). The only new class here is the site validator.

  ===========================================================================
  THE SCATTERER PRECONDITION IS NO LONGER STALE
  ===========================================================================
  This item's own S1/S4/S2 build pass recorded RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces as
  blocking S5 ("miasma's own future work, not this kit's"). That is now
  stale — MIASMA_MECHANICS_1's M6 pass built it for real, and
  SUMP_MECHANICS_1's S3 pass already reused it a second time (both read in
  full before writing this file). SCALD_MECHANICS_1.md's own record is fixed
  in the same pass that adds this file.

  ===========================================================================
  THE VALIDATOR — no stock class does "near a ThingDef"
  ===========================================================================
  RM_ScattererValidator_NearThingDef (new this pass,
  src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/) is the site validator: only
  the mirror-image AVOID case exists in stock
  (Verse.ScattererValidator_AvoidThingsOfDef, read in full) — nothing
  REQUIRES proximity to an existing Thing. thingDef RUT_ScaldVent, radius 6
  (INVENTED — generous enough to cover a vent's own 2x2 footprint plus a
  comfortable "column" margin, without reaching a neighboring vent given
  S4's own intended vent spacing).

  ⚠️ Honest limitation, same shape S4's own header already documents for
  RUT_ScaldVent itself: vent placement is map/world-authoring via the
  bridge, POST-map-generation (RUT_ScaldVent.xml's own header: "NOT worldgen
  ... NOT done this pass"), never a GenStep. So this GenStepDef finds ZERO
  valid sites on the Scald's map exactly as it exists today (no vents
  placed on it yet) — it is real, reachable, wired content that starts
  doing anything the moment S4's own vent placement lands, the same "wired
  ahead of its own precondition" posture RUT_FeverWood_MirrorBreak.xml's own
  header already established for an analogous situation. warnOnFail false
  for precisely this reason, same posture RUT_GenStep_CrecheScatterer's own
  header gives for its own not-yet-everywhere-painted validator.

  minSpacing 10 (> the validator's own radius 6) so a scatter roll cannot
  place two sail-cluster sites inside the same vent's proximity ring —
  approximating "one cluster per vent" without literally iterating the vent
  list (GenStep_Scatterer has no such iteration mode). countPer10kCellsRange
  1.0~1.5 is an intentionally generous ATTEMPT ceiling, not a promise — the
  NearThingDef validator is the real limiter, so an attempt beyond "one per
  reachable vent" simply fails to find a valid cell and costs nothing beyond
  the scatterer's own bounded retry loop. Same "CEILING on attempts, not a
  promise" honesty this item's own S6 wreck scatter already established.

  spotMustBeStandable true, allowInWaterBiome true — RUT_ScaldVent.xml's own
  label calls it "shore-side": standable shore ground is expected within
  the validator's radius, but the biome itself is water-covered overall
  (same allowInWaterBiome true reasoning RUT_ScaldWreckScatter.xml's own
  header already gives for this exact biome).

  anchorMarkerDef deliberately NOT set on the AnchoredPawn element:
  anchoring directly onto RUT_ScaldVent's own 2x2 footprint risks a
  standability/overlap conflict with the vent building itself; the
  element's own documented fallback — anchor to `loc` itself, the scattered
  cell already inside the vent's proximity ring — is the simpler, safer
  choice for "riding the vent's own bubble column" without the pawn needing
  to stand on the vent's own cell.

  pawnKind Penguin (Ludeon.RimWorld Core, vanilla, always loaded) is a
  WIRING PLACEHOLDER, per this task's own instruction not to author the
  real sail kind. Chosen DISTINCT from every other RM_SetPieceElement_
  AnchoredPawn placeholder already claimed in this repo (RSW_OpeeSeaKiller,
  MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M6; Mech_Pikeman, FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F4) to avoid
  ambiguous cross-references — and thematically closer than either: a
  small, already near-nil-combat vanilla animal, unlike those two
  ambush/military picks. Real anchoring does NOT occur with this
  placeholder: Penguin's own ThingDef carries no RM_CompTerritorialAnchor,
  so RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn's own WarningOnce/no-op path fires —
  expected, not a bug, same posture every prior AnchoredPawn placeholder
  consumer already documents inline. Radius 8 (this pass's own INVENTED
  tether value, "never leave their bubble line") is therefore recorded here
  as the value the real sail ThingDef's own CompProperties_
  TerritorialAnchor.anchorRadius should carry once authored — not something
  this pass actually wires live.

  "Never flees, never fights" — confirmed structural, no new C# needed.
  RM_CompTerritorialAnchor itself never calls a JobGiver; it only sets
  pawn.mindState.duty (read in full this pass). Which behavior actually
  runs is entirely the pawn's own ThinkTreeDef's choice: RM_JobGiver_
  AnchorDefense (fight) and RM_JobGiver_AnchorWander (wander) are two
  INDEPENDENT ThinkTreeDef-gated JobGivers, not a package the comp forces
  together. A future sail ThinkTreeDef that includes RM_JobGiver_
  AnchorWander (gated on its own dutyDef) and OMITS RM_JobGiver_
  AnchorDefense entirely gets "wander in the radius, never fight" for free
  — no props flag or third JobGiver class is needed on the comp side. That
  ThinkTreeDef (and the DutyDef it reads, and suppressing vanilla's own
  flee-from-danger branches) is real content authoring tied to the real
  sail ThingDef/PawnKindDef — roster-pass work, not buildable against a
  borrowed placeholder kind, same "compiles now, first XML consumer later"
  posture SUMP_MECHANICS_1's own S3 pass already used for RM_CompStationEater.

  order 975 — after S6's own wreck scatter (965-967) and every terrain-
  generation genStep in this kit; ahead of nothing later in this kit
  depends on sail placement. Should a future pass add a GenStep that
  scatters RUT_ScaldVent itself (rather than hand-placing it), this
  GenStepDef's order must move after it — flagged here for whoever writes
  that later.

  MayRequire mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards: every Class referenced
  (RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces, RM_ScattererValidator_NearThingDef,
  RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn) lives there.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_GenStep_ScaldSailScatterer</defName>
    <order>975</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces">
      <countPer10kCellsRange>1.0~1.5</countPer10kCellsRange>
      <minSpacing>10</minSpacing>
      <spotMustBeStandable>true</spotMustBeStandable>
      <allowInWaterBiome>true</allowInWaterBiome>
      <warnOnFail>false</warnOnFail>
      <validators>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_ScattererValidator_NearThingDef">
          <thingDef>RUT_ScaldVent</thingDef>
          <radius>6</radius>
        </li>
      </validators>
      <elements>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn">
          <!-- WIRING PLACEHOLDER — see this file's own header. Roster pass
               replaces with the real bubble-sailor kind. -->
          <pawnKind>Penguin</pawnKind>
        </li>
      </elements>
    </genStep>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- Mod Settings gate: Terminal Biomes' S5 sail + walker toggle
           (read in RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces.ShouldSkipMap). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_MechanicGateExtension">
        <gateKey>Scald.S5</gateKey>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
